From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Francisco=20Jos=C3=A9=20Garc=C3=ADa=20Garc=C3=ADa?=
 <frangarcj@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:19:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] multidraw: per-cmd vertex stream rebase
 (vglMultiDrawCmd.vertex_base)

Geometrizer's static-mesh path draws ~100 objects/frame whose u16
indices are mesh-relative into a resident 24 MB arena, so each object
needs its interleaved attribute streams rebased to the mesh's first
vertex. Doing that with glVertexAttribPointer + glDrawElements pays
the full per-draw setup every time. Add an optional vertex_base per
vglMultiDrawCmd: NULL leaves the streams alone; non-NULL re-points
every ACTIVE attribute's GXM vertex stream at the new base before the
draw (packed layouts only - the patched vertex program's per-attribute
offsets are stream-relative, no repatch; inactive attributes keep
their constant-value stream, mirroring the IMPL's own stream loop).
cmds[0] must pass NULL and have the GL attrib pointers already bound
to its base, since the first draw's full setup consumes VAO state.

Also document that an over-large top_idx is safe for arena sub-ranges
(it only feeds the zero-copy size decision and the 16-bit index
downgrade) and that the batched uniform must be vertex-stage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/custom_shaders.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++-----
 source/vitaGL.h         | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/custom_shaders.c b/source/custom_shaders.c
index 55fd6ef..f237d00 100644
--- a/source/custom_shaders.c
+++ b/source/custom_shaders.c
@@ -3121,10 +3121,15 @@ void glProgramUniform4fv(GLuint prog, GLint location, GLsizei count, const GLflo
 // vertex default-uniform buffer and copy the whole (small) unif_vbuffer block
 // into it - GXM does not allow writing into a default-uniform-buffer
 // reservation again once a prior sceGxmDraw has consumed it, so this
-// reserve+copy must happen once per draw - and (c) issue sceGxmDraw directly
-// with that draw's indices/count. No texture, attribute or vertex-program
-// state changes between draws in this entry point, so none of that work is
-// repeated.
+// reserve+copy must happen once per draw - (c) if the cmd carries a
+// non-NULL vertex_base, rebase every ACTIVE attribute's GXM vertex stream
+// to it (packed/interleaved layouts only: the patched vertex program's
+// per-attribute offsets are stream-relative, so an address change needs no
+// repatch; inactive attributes keep their constant-value stream, mirroring
+// the active/inactive split of the IMPL's own sceGxmSetVertexStream loop) -
+// and (d) issue sceGxmDraw directly with that draw's indices/count. No
+// texture or vertex-program state changes between draws in this entry
+// point, so none of that work is repeated.
 void vglMultiDrawElementsUniform4fv(GLenum mode, GLint uniform_location,
 		GLsizei uniform_vec4_count, const vglMultiDrawCmd *cmds, GLsizei n,
 		GLuint top_idx) {
@@ -3190,7 +3195,8 @@ void vglMultiDrawElementsUniform4fv(GLenum mode, GLint uniform_location,
 		sceGxmDraw(gxm_context, gxm_p, SCE_GXM_INDEX_FORMAT_U16, ptr, count);
 	}
 
-	// --- cmds[1..n-1]: uniform reseed + fresh default-uniform-buffer + draw. ---
+	// --- cmds[1..n-1]: uniform reseed + fresh default-uniform-buffer +
+	// optional vertex stream rebase + draw. ---
 	for (GLsizei i = 1; i < n; i++) {
 		vgl_fill_uniform_data(cmds[i].uniform_data, SCE_GXM_PARAMETER_TYPE_F32, 4, uniform_vec4_count)
 
@@ -3200,6 +3206,14 @@ void vglMultiDrawElementsUniform4fv(GLenum mode, GLint uniform_location,
 			dirty_shader_vert_unifs = GL_FALSE;
 		}
 
+		if (cmds[i].vertex_base) {
+			for (int j = 0; j < p->attr_num; j++) {
+				uint8_t attr_idx = p->attr_map[j];
+				if (cur_vao->vertex_attrib_state & (1 << attr_idx))
+					sceGxmSetVertexStream(gxm_context, j, cmds[i].vertex_base);
+			}
+		}
+
 		const void *idx_i = gpu_buf ? (const void *)((uint8_t *)gpu_buf->ptr + (uint32_t)cmds[i].indices)
 		                            : cmds[i].indices;
 		if (gpu_buf)
diff --git a/source/vitaGL.h b/source/vitaGL.h
index 0260b89..d0dbb2d 100644
--- a/source/vitaGL.h
+++ b/source/vitaGL.h
@@ -1077,6 +1077,12 @@ typedef struct {
 	const void *indices;        // GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT index list for this draw
 	int32_t count;               // index count for this draw
 	const float *uniform_data;   // uniform_vec4_count vec4s (uniform_vec4_count * 4 floats) to upload before this draw
+	const void *vertex_base;     // NULL = vertex streams unchanged; non-NULL = rebase every ACTIVE
+	                             // attribute's vertex stream to this (GPU-mapped) pointer before this
+	                             // draw. For interleaved/packed attribute layouts only: the patched
+	                             // vertex program keeps its per-attribute intra-stride offsets, so a
+	                             // stream-address change needs no repatch. MUST be NULL for cmds[0]
+	                             // (see the function comment below).
 } vglMultiDrawCmd;
 
 // Batches a run of glUniform4fv(uniform_location, uniform_vec4_count, ...) +
@@ -1086,14 +1092,30 @@ typedef struct {
 // glDrawElements/_glDrawElements_CustomShadersIMPL normally redoes on every
 // call (fragment/vertex texture binds, attribute alignment + packing
 // analysis, vertex program patching, and the top-index scan) runs once for
-// the whole batch instead of once per draw; only the uniform data and the
+// the whole batch instead of once per draw; only the uniform data, the
 // GXM default-uniform-buffer reservation (which GXM requires fresh per draw)
-// are repeated for cmds[1..n-1].
+// and the optional vertex_base stream rebase are repeated for cmds[1..n-1].
+//
+// cmds[0] contract: its vertex_base must be NULL and the caller must have
+// the GL vertex attrib pointers (glVertexAttribPointer / VAO state) already
+// bound to cmds[0]'s vertex base - the first draw goes through the full
+// setup path, which consumes that GL-side state to program the GXM streams;
+// vertex_base is ignored on cmds[0].
+//
+// The batched uniform must be a VERTEX-stage uniform: cmds[1..n-1] only
+// re-reserve and re-upload the vertex default uniform buffer. If the named
+// uniform aliases into the fragment program too, the fragment side is only
+// refreshed by cmds[0].
+//
 // top_idx is the highest vertex index referenced by ANY cmd in the batch,
 // plus 1 - the caller must know this already (eg. the vertex count of a
 // shared/fused vertex buffer), which is what lets this entry point skip the
 // O(indices) index high-water scan that the single-draw path has to do when
-// it isn't told.
+// it isn't told. Passing an over-large top_idx (eg. the max vertex count
+// over several sub-ranges of a resident arena when cmds rebase between
+// them) is safe and intentional: it only feeds the zero-copy-vs-temp-copy
+// size decision (SAFER_DRAW_SPEEDHACK threshold) and the 16-bit index-source
+// downgrade - the GPU only dereferences indices the draws actually contain.
 void vglMultiDrawElementsUniform4fv(GLenum mode, GLint uniform_location,
 	GLsizei uniform_vec4_count, const vglMultiDrawCmd *cmds, GLsizei n,
 	GLuint top_idx);
